course: dictionary
lesson: 13317
title: The grocer
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A grocer is a person who owns or runs a shop that sells food and things for the home, such as tea, sugar, tins and cleaning things. «Mum sent me to the grocer for tea and sugar.» The word tells you who runs the shop, and the things they sell tell you what kind of shop it is.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence: tea, sugar and food all go with a shop that sells groceries. Groceries are everyday things we buy to eat and to use at home. So a grocer is the person who sells them.
explain: Sometimes grocer means the shop itself. In the UK you might say «the grocer's», and in the US you would say «the grocery store». Both mean the same kind of place, so the sentence around the word tells you which meaning is meant.
fact: A grocer is a person who owns or runs a shop that sells food and things for the home.
fact: «The grocer's» means the shop itself in the UK.
fact: «Grocery store» means the same kind of shop in the US.
fact: In old village life, the grocer was often a corner shop owner who weighed out sugar and tea.
fact: Today most people shop in supermarkets, but the word grocer is still used.
exercise: «The grocer weighed out a kilo of apples for me.» Who weighed the apples? | The postman | *The grocer | The farmer | The baker
exercise: What does a grocer sell? | Shoes and hats | Books and maps | *Tea, sugar and tins | Cars and bicycles
exercise: «Mum bought tea, sugar and tins from the grocer.» Find and copy one word that names something sold at the grocer's. | bought | *tea | mum | from
test: In the UK, what does «the grocer's» mean? | A school for maths | A bus stop | *The shop itself | A type of tea
test: Which shop would a grocer run? | A shop that sells only shoes | A shop that sells only flowers | A shop that fixes cars | *A shop that sells food and things for the home
exam: «The grocer sold tins, tea and sugar, and gave change to the children.» What does the grocer do in this sentence? | Bakes bread in an oven | *Sells food and home things, and gives change | Teaches the children to swim | Only fixes bicycles
